# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two goals:
#   1. Keep the context small (a `target/` directory is easily several GB).
#   2. Keep the context STABLE. Every byte sent to the daemon participates in
#      BuildKit's cache keys, so excluding files the build never reads means
#      editing a doc or a script does not invalidate a single build layer.
#
# Anything the build genuinely needs must NOT appear here. In particular:
#   - Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock / crates/ / apps/  (Rust build + cargo-chef recipe)
#   - apps/cogwheel-web/package*.json + src/     (web bundle)

# --- VCS and CI -------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
target
**/target
**/node_modules
apps/cogwheel-web/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# --- Runtime state and secrets ----------------------------------------------
# `.env` is how compose passes real config; it must never be baked into a layer.
data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Documentation and deployment assets ------------------------------------
# None of this is read by the build; excluding it keeps doc edits from
# busting the Rust and web layers.
*.md
docs
deploy
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- scripts ----------------------------------------------------------------
# All but one, and the exception is deliberate: the runtime image carries
# verify-install.sh so a container-only host (Unraid, a plain `docker run`)
# can check its own install with `docker exec`. The COPY for it sits after the
# expensive layers, so editing the script rebuilds only image metadata.
#
# `scripts/*` rather than `scripts`: a negation cannot re-include a file from a
# directory that was excluded whole.
scripts/*
!scripts/verify-install.sh

# --- Editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.swp
